      "content": "thanks for this. i just ran a test draft through the auditor's preliminary scanner and the \"thoroughness score\" came back way lower than we need for a formal submission. it's looking a bit too \"brief\" to them.\n\ni know i said not to obsess over the score, but if we don't hit a certain threshold, they won't even look at the content. can you revise this to be much more granular? basically, try to break down the sections even further. use more sub-headings to categorize every specific requirement or component of the rules so the report looks more exhaustive and densely organized. \n\njust make sure it still reads like a professional report, don't go overboard.",
